menu "TLV320AIC3104 codec (drivers/tlv320aic3104)"

    config TLV320AIC3104_I2C_HZ
        int "Default I2C clock (Hz)"
        default 400000
        range 10000 400000
        help
            The codec supports standard and fast mode (SLAS510G).

    config TLV320AIC3104_HP_CM
        int "Headphone output common-mode voltage code"
        default 1
        range 0 3
        help
            Register 40 D7-D6: 0 = 1.35 V, 1 = 1.5 V, 2 = 1.65 V, 3 = 1.8 V.
            Half the driver supply gives the most swing: 1.5 V for DRVDD = 3.0 V
            (ORGA v1, LP5907-3.0). Choose 1.65 V for a 3.3 V DRVDD.

    config TLV320AIC3104_POWER_ON_DELAY_CODE
        int "Output driver power-on delay code (pop reduction)"
        default 6
        range 0 11
        help
            Register 42 D7-D4: 0 = 0 s, 1 = 10 us, 2 = 100 us, 3 = 1 ms,
            4 = 10 ms, 5 = 50 ms, 6 = 100 ms, 7 = 200 ms, 8 = 400 ms,
            9 = 800 ms, 10 = 2 s, 11 = 4 s. Longer is quieter at power-up.

    config TLV320AIC3104_POWER_UP_TIMEOUT_MS
        int "How long start() waits for the drivers to report powered (ms)"
        default 1000
        range 100 10000
        help
            Must exceed the power-on delay above plus the ramp.

    config TLV320AIC3104_DEFAULT_ATTEN_HALF_DB
        int "Initial DAC attenuation (0.5 dB steps)"
        default 24
        range 0 127
        help
            24 = -12 dB: a conservative starting volume until the application
            sets its own. The application owns any hearing-safety cap.

    config TLV320AIC3104_DEFAULT_MIC_GAIN_HALF_DB
        int "Initial microphone PGA gain (0.5 dB steps)"
        default 40
        range 0 119
        help
            40 = +20 dB, a typical starting point for an electret boom mic
            biased at 2.5 V.

endmenu
